{"name":"Baptism by Fire","hex":"#e6490b","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baptism by fire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rite of passage through the survival or success of a crisis or ordeal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baptism_by_fire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baptism by fire","blocks":[{"text":"The phrase baptism by fire, baptism of fire or baptism with fire is a Christian theological concept originating from the words of John the Baptist in Matthew 3:11."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baptism_by_fire","wikidata":"Q1409751"},{"title":"By Fire","blocks":[{"text":"\"By Fire\" is the sixth episode of the second season and 28th episode overall from the FOX series Gotham. The episode was written by Rebecca Perry Cutter and directed by TJ Scott. It was first broadcast on October 26, 2015, in FOX. Continuing from the previous episode, Bridgit Pike decides to kill her brothers after being abused, going into a vigilante crusade, forcing Gordon to stop her with the help from Selina Kyle. Kringle's and Edward Nygma's relationship turns into a tragedy, while Penguin decides to free his mother from Theo Galavan's clutches."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/By_Fire","wikidata":"Q23419161"},{"title":"Baptism","blocks":[{"text":"Baptism is a Christian rite of initiation almost invariably with the use of water. It may be performed by sprinkling or pouring water on the head, or immersing in water, traditionally three times for each person of the Trinity. It is also called christening, although this is typically reserved for the baptism of infants. Baptism is regarded as a sacrament in most churches and an ordinance in others. The synoptic Gospels recount that John the Baptist baptized Jesus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/The_Baptism_of_Christ_%28Verrocchio_%26_Leonardo%29.jpg/330px-The_Baptism_of_Christ_%28Verrocchio_%26_Leonardo%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&